DATABENTO_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE

# --- Usage tracking (optional, off by default) --------------------------------
# How much time the app gets, in minutes, to PostHog. The browser beats once a
# minute while a tab is visible and you have touched something in the last five,
# so one event is one minute and the count IS the duration; the `section`
# property splits it by tab (Replay / Live / Trades / Research / ...).
# See frontend/src/lib/activity.ts for what is and is not sent.
#
# UNSET MEANS OFF, and off is the default: posthog-js is never imported and the
# frontend makes no external requests whatsoever. Setting this is the only thing
# in the repo that sends anything off the machine, so set it deliberately.
# Autocapture and session recording are both disabled in code — element text in
# this app is P&L and trade dates — so what leaves is the beat, the workspace
# and the tab path. Events are anonymous: totals add up across devices (desktop,
# phone on the tailnet) with no identity wired, at the cost of double-counting
# minutes when two of them are open at once.
#
# Free tier is 1M events/month against roughly 7k for four hours a day; set a
# billing limit in PostHog if you want that guaranteed. Free-plan retention is
# one year, after which data moves to cold storage.
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_YOUR_PROJECT_KEY
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com   # default is US cloud

# AI analyzer — LiteLLM model strings. LLM_MODEL is the default; LLM_MODELS is a
# comma-separated list of models you can pick between to compare reviews
# (Claude vs ChatGPT vs DeepSeek, etc.). Set each provider's API key below;
# LiteLLM reads them from the environment.
LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
LLM_MODELS=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6,openai/gpt-4o,deepseek/deepseek-chat
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE
# OPENAI_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE

# Rithmic — live shadow mode (docs/live-shadow-plan.md). Market data by default;
# the ORDER plant is opened only by the routing block further down, and only when
# every key there is set deliberately.
# `python demo/rithmic_smoke.py --discover` needs no credentials and prints
# every gateway with the systems it serves — use it to fill in the two below.
# RITHMIC_GATEWAY is host:port; rprotocol.rithmic.com:443 is the generic
# production entry point, ritpz06001.rithmic.com:443 is Singapore (nearest KL),
# rituz00100.rithmic.com:443 is the test gateway (system_name "Rithmic Test").
# RITHMIC_SYSTEM_NAME must match a name that gateway advertises, verbatim.
# RITHMIC_APP_NAME must be the app name Rithmic certified for you, if you have
# been through conformance.
# RITHMIC_USER=YOUR_LOGIN_HERE
# RITHMIC_PASSWORD=YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE
# RITHMIC_SYSTEM_NAME=Rithmic Test
# RITHMIC_GATEWAY=rituz00100.rithmic.com:443
# RITHMIC_APP_NAME=atas_journal_shadow
# RITHMIC_APP_VERSION=0.1
#
# RITHMIC_AGGREGATED_QUOTES asks Rithmic to coalesce quotes instead of sending
# the tape print for print. It is set on the login itself (RequestLogin), so it
# is chosen once per connection and applies to the ticker and history plants;
# the order plant never sees it. Unset means off, and off is what this repo
# wants: an aggregated row stands for several trades, which quietly breaks
# big-lot detection, the fill model's queue estimate, and any size distribution
# read off a recorded session (backfill bars start arriving with num_trades > 1,
# counted as `backfill_aggregated` in the feed's stats). Turn it on only to cut
# CPU on a machine reading candles, or to match an R|Trader Pro session that has
# it on — two connections whose tapes you intend to compare must agree, which is
# the same rule ATAS states for its own Rithmic connector. The feed reports the
# mode it connected in as `aggregated_quotes` in /live status.
# RITHMIC_AGGREGATED_QUOTES=1

# Live shadow mode on startup. LIVE_SYMBOL must be a RAW contract (NQU6), never
# a root: a root sends contract_for() to probe Databento, which a live path must
# never do, and the on-disk roll map ends 2026-06-30 anyway.
# With LIVE_AUTOSTART unset the API still *resumes* a session already recorded
# for today (rebuilding the tape from data/live/ticks/) — it just does not open
# a connection or start writing. Turn autostart on only on the always-on host.
# LIVE_AUTOSTART=1
# LIVE_SYMBOL=NQU6
# LIVE_EXCHANGE=CME

# --- Order routing (Phase 7) -------------------------------------------------
# ONE variable, and everything else about routing is set in the app where you
# can see it. It used to be five keys with dependencies between them, which is
# a thing nobody remembers correctly at 09:31.
#
# LIVE_ROUTING makes the routing endpoints reachable at all. Without it every one
# of them answers 403 with this variable's name in the message, and Rithmic's
# ORDER plant is never opened. It is the deployment-level "this machine must
# never trade" — the always-on host wants it unset, and no amount of clicking in
# the UI can undo that. Shadow mode does not need it, and neither does paper
# trading on the chart, which works without it.
#
# What moved into the app:
#   - which kind each account is (demo/live) — a per-account label you set once
#     in the order-entry panel, shown as a badge everywhere the account appears.
#     Nothing Rithmic sends says whether an account is funded, so it is somebody's
#     declaration either way; this way it is a visible one. An UNLABELLED account
#     cannot send anything — there is no default, because the wrong default is
#     an order on a funded account.
#   - which account to route to — the selector, which also holds "Paper". Every
#     session starts on Paper, including after a restart or the 18:00 roll.
#   - one-click trading (skip the confirm popup) — per account, off by default,
#     and cleared automatically whenever an account is labelled live.
#   There is no per-order quantity ceiling. How large an order may be is
#   max_risk_usd's question — a guardrail level, in dollars on the contract
#   being sent to — because the same five contracts is $125 of MNQ and $1,250
#   of NQ and a number of lots cannot tell them apart.
# LIVE_ROUTING=1

# LIVE_GUARDRAILS is the discipline layer — the daily stop, the slow-down
# threshold, the minimum target, the stop-width clamp. Its levels come from
# docs/research/lucidpro-operating-plan.md, which fits them to this trader's own
# 2,538 round trips rather than to generic prop advice.
#
# UNLIKE LIVE_ROUTING IT IS ON UNLESS YOU SWITCH IT OFF. Unset means enforced;
# only an explicit 0/false/no/off disables it. The two flags point opposite ways
# on purpose — the safe default for a permission is "denied" and the safe default
# for a restraint is "enforced", and both of those fail toward not losing money.
#
# It lives out here, and not in the app, because that IS the feature: turning the
# rules off should mean leaving the chart, not reaching a toggle beside the order
# pad at 09:31 with a red P&L. The levels themselves are order-entry settings —
# set any one of them to 0 to disable that rule alone — and this is only the
# master switch. While it is off the chart's top bar says so in red, because a
# safety layer that is silently off is worse than one that was never built.
#
# None of this is un-bypassable by whoever owns the machine. It buys friction and
# visibility, not impossibility.
# LIVE_GUARDRAILS=0

# REPLAY_GUARDRAILS is the same layer on /replay, where the money is imaginary —
# the browser applying its own mirror of the rules (frontend/src/lib/guardRules.ts)
# so that practice refuses what the funded account refuses. Same polarity: unset
# means enforced, only an explicit 0/false/no/off turns it off.
#
# It is a SEPARATE switch from LIVE_GUARDRAILS and neither implies the other,
# because they protect different things. The live flag protects an account; this
# one protects a habit — and the replay is also the only place cheap enough to
# TEST a rule, which a rule that forbids its own test can never be. Switch it off
# to run a session the rules would not allow: a 30-tick stop, an 80-tick target,
# trading past the daily stop to see what the rest of the day did.
#
# Off, nothing is refused and nothing is auto-flattened — but every rule is still
# computed and still shown, and the discipline strip says in red that it is not
# enforcing. Restart the API after changing this; the page reads it from
# /live/routing, which is also where the levels come from.
# REPLAY_GUARDRAILS=0
